# Target C: five-no-root slack-two reduction

Date: 2026-09-20

Status: exact strengthening of one five-no-root branch plus a deletion reduction for the six-no-root layer. This does not yet prove the six-no-root density inequality, does not reduce the 3,874-state generic-H6 endpoint, and does not close C-II.

New companion verifier:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_five_noroot_k4_p5_slack_2026_09_20.py`

## Defect notation

Write

`D(A) = |A| - 3 delta(A)`

with

`delta(A) = r_M(A) - r_Q(A)`.

The committed work proves `D(A)>=0` for every family with at most five no-root four-cycles. The next direct density layer is six no-root cycles.

There is a useful stronger target at five no-root cycles:

> prove `D(A)>=2` for every five-no-root family.

That stronger statement would close the entire six-no-root factor-three problem without a 325,911-orbit six-no-root local-state scan.

## Deletion lemma

Let `e` be one selected row of `A`, and put `A'=A\{e}`. Since `Q` is a quotient of `M`, deleting one row loses at least as much rank in `M` as in `Q`. Hence

`m_e = delta(A) - delta(A')`

lies in `{0,1}`. Therefore

`D(A') = D(A) - 1 + 3 m_e`.

Now suppose `A` has exactly six no-root rows and `D(A)<0`. Delete any one of those six no-root rows. The resulting family has exactly five no-root rows.

If `m_e=0`, then

`D(A') = D(A)-1 < 0`.

If `m_e=1`, then

`D(A') = D(A)+2 <= 1`.

Thus the five-no-root bound `D>=2` would contradict either possibility. Consequently:

> If every five-no-root family has `D>=2`, then every six-no-root family has `D>=0`.

So a five-no-root slack-two theorem is a sufficient certificate for the full six-no-root density layer.

## New k=4,p=5 exact audit

The committed five-no-root `k=4` containment theorem uses a virtual canonical rank-one coefficient space `P`. Let `C` be its canonical complete-block set,

`c=|C|`,

and

`d = c - rank H(C)`.

For every compatible actual state, if `q` canonical-complete blocks are replaced by incomplete states and `p` is the total number of selected root-0 rows in incomplete blocks, the theorem gives

`D(A) >= 5 + p + 3d - 3q`,

with

`d>=2`

and

`q<=p`.

For `p<=4` this already gives `D>=3`. At `p=5`, the only way the lower bound can be below two is the equality pattern

`(d,q,p)=(2,5,5)`.

Because `q=p=5`, all five replaced canonical-complete blocks must be compatible singletons; there is no row budget left for any other incomplete block.

The new verifier exhausts this equality pattern over the exact 20,451 `S_7` orbits and the same 177,316 virtual canonical rank-one states used by the containment theorem.

There are 342 canonical states with `d=2`. Only nine have at least five canonical-complete blocks admitting a compatible singleton. These produce exactly 44 five-singleton choices. All 44 choices actually realize the target line `P`.

Every one is reranked directly over `Q`. The exact census is

```text
|A|   delta(A)   D(A)   states
22       4        10       2
25       5        10      42
```

Thus the apparent `D=1` boundary at `p=5` is absent; the minimum exact defect in the only potentially sub-two case is 10.

## k=4,p<=6 now has uniform slack two

The new `p=5` audit combines with the already committed `p=6` residual audit.

At `p=6`, the containment lower bound can fall below two only for

`(d,q,p)=(2,6,6)`.

The existing verifier found exactly seven realizable states of that form and reranked all seven exactly. Every one has

`|A|=23`, `delta(A)=4`, `D(A)=11`.

Every other `p=6` state has containment lower bound at least two. Therefore:

> Every five-no-root `k=4,p<=6` family satisfies `D(A)>=2`.

This is stronger than the previously recorded factor-three statement `D(A)>=0` for that branch.

## Exact remaining slack-two bands at t=5

The crude bound for five no-root rows is

`D(A) >= 5 + p - 3k`.

Therefore a state with `D<2` can occur only in the following ranges:

- `k=2`: `p<=2`;
- `k=3`: `p<=5`;
- `k=4`: `p<=8`;
- `k=5`: `p<=11`.

Existing exact work already gives slack two for

- `k=2,p=0`;
- `k=3,p<=3`;
- `k=4,p<=6` after the new audit above.

The remaining five-no-root slack-two target is therefore reduced to

- `k=2,p=1,2`;
- `k=3,p=4,5`;
- `k=4,p=7,8`;
- `k=5,p<=11`.

For `k=5,p<=9`, factor-three nonnegativity is already proved, but the earlier verifier was designed to exclude negative defect rather than exclude defect 0 or 1. Those cases must be audited before the deletion lemma can be invoked.

This slack-two program may be cheaper than attacking 325,911 six-no-root orbits directly. The next small targets are `k=2,p=1,2` and `k=3,p=4,5`, where the existing canonical constraint-space machinery already supplies most of the reduction.

## Direct C-II bottleneck

This remains an auxiliary metric-basis route. The direct generic-H6 endpoint is still

`3874 = 3076 C7 + 798 (C3 disjoint-union C4)`.

The state-specific exact forced-segment-order scan remains the computation most directly capable of removing those cells, followed by quantitative sine-law metric compatibility for survivors. No theorem-state authority file is changed by this result.
